          "annotations": [],
          "text": "{\"stories\":[{\"id\":\"s000014\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"A clear flood emergency, false blame, and partial grain rescue unfold logically; the sober, unresolved ending is vivid but more adult and bleak than ideal for young children.\" ,\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000028\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The inaccessible diagram and unsafe gate create a coherent constraint, while the saved sacks and submerged step provide a concrete partial-resolution ending.\" ,\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000038\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The inaccessible diagram and unsafe gate create a coherent constraint, while the saved sacks and submerged step provide a concrete partial-resolution ending.\" ,\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000023\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The inaccessible diagram and unsafe gate create a coherent constraint, while the saved sacks and submerged step provide a concrete partial-resolution ending.\" ,\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000017\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"Ida learns the lift-and-brace sequence through the small sluice test, but cannot operate the dangerous gate alone; the grain-count ending makes the partial loss tangible.\" ,\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000021\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The inaccessible diagram and unsafe gate create a coherent constraint, while the saved sacks and submerged step provide a concrete partial-resolution ending.\" ,\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000002\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"Ida's distracted reading leaves her unable to use the lever safely, leading coherently to a partial rescue and the image of water swallowing the step.\" ,\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000037\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The inaccessible diagram and unsafe gate create a coherent constraint, while the saved sacks and submerged step provide a concrete partial-resolution ending.\" ,\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000024\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":7},\"note\":\"The inaccessible diagram and unsafe gate create a coherent constraint, while the saved sacks and submerged step provide a concrete partial-resolution ending.\" ,\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000019\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"Ida learns the lift-and-brace sequence through the small sluice test, but cannot operate the dangerous gate alone; the grain-count ending makes the partial loss tangible.\" ,\"group_id\":0}],\"diversity\":{\"premise\":1,\"causal_path\":2,\"ending\":0,\"language\":1,\"overall\":1},\"diversity_evidence\":\"All ten stories share the same flooded grain-store emergency, Ren's wrongful blame and clearing, bent retaining pin, partial rescue of twenty-four sacks, and identical flooded-step ending. s000017 and s000019 add a successful sluice test, while s000014 and s000002 use incomplete reading and s000028, s000038, s000023, s000021, s000037, and s000024 use an inaccessible diagram; these are minor route variations within one plot.\",\"plot_groups\":[{\"group_id\":0,\"summary\":\"A jammed mill gate threatens winter grain; Ida clears newcomer Ren of blame but lacks either instructions or enough safe help to repair it, so the group saves some sacks while the flood spoils the rest.\"}]}",
